From: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw89: keep the RX settings without BT on eFEM boards

rtw8852c_btc_set_rfe() takes an even RFE type for a module with a
dedicated BT antenna. The coex then runs at the non-shared-antenna trx
level, whose RX gain setting calls ctrl_nbtg_bt_tx(true): it forces the
RX FIR type and changes the RX baseband and LNA settings. On the
RTL8852CE this stops all reception at 80 and 160 MHz.

Boards with an external FEM (RFE type above 50) are access points
without BT, and the vendor driver leaves the FIR type alone on them.
Keep the default RX settings there.

Signed-off-by: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/rtw8852c.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/rtw8852c.c
@@ -3068,6 +3068,12 @@ static void rtw8852c_btc_set_wl_rx_gain(
 {
 	struct rtw89_btc *btc = &rtwdev->btc;
 
+	/* eFEM boards have no BT. The BT free-run RX settings force the RX
+	 * FIR type, which stops all reception at 80 and 160 MHz.
+	 */
+	if (rtw89_rfe_has_efem(rtwdev))
+		level = 0;
+
 	switch (level) {
 	case 0: /* original */
 	default:
